---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBand from '../../components/layout/ContactBand.astro';
import SmithManoeuvreCalculator from '../../components/calculators/SmithManoeuvreCalculator.astro';

const title = 'Smith Manoeuvre Model';
const description = 'A calculator for comparing leveraged and non-leveraged investing outcomes under different debt, investment, and tax assumptions.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/work/smith-manoeuvre">
  <article class="smith-page">
    <header class="smith-hero page-shell">
      <div class="smith-hero-copy">
        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <p class="hero-dek">I built the model to compare a Smith Manoeuvre investing strategy with a non-leveraged alternative, then kept refining it to better estimate how the incremental benefits and costs change under different assumptions.</p>
      </div>

    </header>

    <section class="case-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="strategy-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">The strategy</p>
        <h2 id="strategy-title">What is the Smith Manoeuvre?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-copy reading-copy--single">
        <p>The Smith Manoeuvre is a Canadian debt-conversion and leveraged-investing strategy built around a readvanceable mortgage. Mortgage interest paid on a personal residence is generally not tax deductible in Canada. Interest on money borrowed for an income-earning purpose can be deductible. The strategy uses that distinction to gradually replace regular mortgage debt with investment borrowing.</p>
        <p>In simplified terms, each mortgage payment pays down principal and creates new room on the linked HELOC. That room can be borrowed back and invested in a taxable portfolio. If the borrowing qualifies for interest deductibility, the resulting tax savings can be directed back toward the mortgage, creating more room to borrow and invest again.</p>
        <p>This page models a simplified version of that process. Leveraged investing adds market, borrowing, and psychological risk. Use the calculator to explore the mechanics, but do not make financial decisions based on its outputs. Anyone seriously considering the strategy should do much deeper research and get tax and financial advice from a professional.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="calculator-section" aria-labelledby="calculator-title">
      <div class="page-shell calculator-intro">
        <p class="section-kicker">Calculator</p>
        <h2 id="calculator-title">Explore a scenario</h2>
      </div>
      <SmithManoeuvreCalculator />
    </section>

    <section class="case-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="model-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">The model</p>
        <h2 id="model-title">How the model works</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-copy reading-copy--single">
        <p>The strategy combines a mortgage, a readvanceable line of credit, leveraged investing, borrowing costs, and tax assumptions. As the mortgage principal falls, eligible borrowing room can be redrawn and invested, so the model has to track both the growing portfolio and the debt used to finance it.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mechanism-flowline">Mortgage payment → principal repaid → available HELOC room → investment draw → portfolio → HELOC interest → estimated tax offset</p>
    </section>

    <section class="fairness-section" aria-labelledby="fairness-title">
      <div class="page-shell fairness-inner">
        <div class="fairness-copy">
          <h2 id="fairness-title">Making the comparison fair</h2>
          <p>If one scenario gets to use a dollar and the other one never receives it, the difference is coming from the spreadsheet rather than the strategy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cash-identity" aria-label="Equal external household cash comparison">
          <div class="cash-path"><p class="cash-label">Smith household cash</p><p class="cash-equation">fixed mortgage cash budget + HELOC interest</p></div>
          <div class="cash-divider" aria-hidden="true">=</div>
          <div class="cash-path"><p class="cash-label">Baseline household cash</p><p class="cash-equation">fixed mortgage cash budget + matching investment equal to HELOC interest</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="fairness-footnote">Any unused mortgage-payment cash is also kept productive in both scenarios rather than disappearing from the comparison.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="public-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">Public calculator</p>
        <h2 id="public-title">Simplifying the model for the web</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-copy reading-copy--single">
        <p>The original spreadsheet was more detailed than I wanted a public calculator to be. For the web version, I rebuilt the comparison as a monthly model with fewer assumptions, an explicit equal-cash baseline, and conservative borrowing limits.</p>
      </div>
      <details class="assumption-details">
        <summary>Calculation assumptions</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Mortgage payments use the Canadian fixed-rate semi-annual convention.</li>
          <li>HELOC interest is modeled monthly on the opening balance.</li>
          <li>New HELOC borrowing is limited by actual principal reduction and available revolving room.</li>
          <li>The illustrative tax-offset proxy assumes 100% of modeled HELOC interest is eligible and applies the marginal tax-rate proxy. That is a modeling assumption, not a determination of actual tax eligibility.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </section>


    <section class="case-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">Limitations</p>
        <h2 id="limits-title">What the model leaves out</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-copy reading-copy--single">
        <p>The model holds the home value, borrowing rates, and investment return constant within each scenario. It simplifies HELOC interest and tax treatment and does not model fees, full tax rules, lender-specific products, or market volatility.</p>
        <p>Actual borrowing availability and interest deductibility depend on individual circumstances, lender terms, and current rules. Borrowing to invest also increases exposure to both market losses and changes in borrowing costs.</p>
        <p><strong>Educational scenario model only. Not financial, tax, legal, or lending advice.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <details class="assumption-details">
        <summary>Detailed assumptions and limitations</summary>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div><h3>Tax</h3><p>The estimated tax offset is only an illustration. The public UI fixes the model assumption at 100% of modeled HELOC interest eligible before applying the marginal tax-rate proxy. Actual deductibility depends on the use and tracing of borrowed funds, income-earning purpose, legal obligations, record keeping, and other tax rules. This calculator does not determine tax eligibility.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Lending</h3><p>The educational model uses simplified borrowing boundaries. Actual HELOC limits, combined-loan rules, underwriting, payments, and readvancement behaviour depend on the lender and current requirements.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Mortgage mechanics</h3><p>The mortgage calculation is a standardized monthly illustration. Actual payment timing, prepayment privileges, variable-rate mechanics, fees, and lender calculations may differ.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Investment risk</h3><p>Borrowing to invest increases exposure to both market losses and interest-rate changes. Returns are uncertain, borrowing costs can rise, and investments can underperform borrowing costs for long periods.</p></div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="workbook-section" aria-labelledby="workbook-title">
      <div class="page-shell workbook-inner">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Workbook</p>
          <h2 id="workbook-title">Download the workbook</h2>
          <p>The workbook uses hypothetical inputs and follows the same monthly calculation structure as the public calculator.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="download-link" href="/downloads/Smith_Manoeuvre_Public_Sanitized_V2.xlsx" download>Download workbook <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
  <ContactBand />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .smith-page { overflow: clip; }
  .page-shell { width: min(calc(100% - 2.25rem), var(--content-main)); margin-inline: auto; }
  .smith-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.4fr) minmax(18rem,.6fr); gap: clamp(2.5rem,6vw,6.5rem); align-items: end; padding-block: clamp(3.75rem,8vw,7.5rem) clamp(4.5rem,8vw,7rem); }
  .section-kicker, .cash-label { margin: 0; font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 760; letter-spacing: .12em; line-height: 1.2; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .section-kicker { color: var(--color-teal); }
  .smith-hero h1 { max-width: 58rem; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(3.35rem,7vw,6.6rem); line-height: .94; letter-spacing: -.065em; }
  .hero-dek { max-width: 50rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: clamp(1.08rem,1.8vw,1.35rem); line-height: 1.54; }
  .proof-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong); }
  .proof-grid div { min-width: 0; padding: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong); }
  .proof-grid dt { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 720; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .proof-grid dd { margin: .38rem 0 0; color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 710; }
  .case-section { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem,8vw,7.5rem); }
  .section-heading { max-width: 58rem; }
  .section-heading h2, .fairness-copy h2, .calculator-intro h2, .qa-copy h2, .workbook-inner h2 { margin: .65rem 0 0; color: var(--color-ink); font-size: clamp(2.2rem,4.2vw,4rem); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .reading-copy { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: clamp(1.5rem,4vw,4rem); max-width: 69rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .reading-copy--single { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: var(--content-reading); }
  .case-section[aria-labelledby="strategy-title"] > .reading-copy--single,
  .case-section[aria-labelledby="limits-title"] > .reading-copy--single { max-width: min(46rem, 100%); gap: clamp(1rem,1.3vw,1.25rem); }
  .case-section[aria-labelledby="public-title"] > .section-heading,
  .case-section[aria-labelledby="public-title"] > .section-heading h2 { max-width: min(72rem, 100%); }
  .reading-copy p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: clamp(1rem,1.25vw,1.12rem); line-height: 1.7; }
  .mechanism-flowline { margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-line); background: var(--color-surface); color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 760; line-height: 1.8; }
  .calculator-section { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem,8vw,7.5rem); background: var(--color-surface-soft); }
  .calculator-intro > p:not(.section-kicker) { max-width: 50rem; color: var(--color-text); }
  .privacy-line { font-weight: 760; }
  .fairness-section { background: var(--color-deep-teal); color: var(--color-on-deep); }
  .fairness-inner { padding-block: clamp(4.75rem,8vw,7.5rem); }
  .fairness-copy h2 { color: var(--color-on-deep); }
  .fairness-copy p { max-width: 50rem; color: var(--color-on-deep-muted); }
  .cash-identity { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) auto minmax(0,1fr); gap: clamp(1rem,3vw,2.5rem); align-items: center; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .cash-path { padding: clamp(1.35rem,3vw,2rem); border: 1px solid rgb(199 218 215 / .35); border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
  .cash-label { color: var(--color-on-deep-muted); }
  .cash-equation { margin: .7rem 0 0; font-weight: 700; }
  .cash-divider { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .fairness-footnote { max-width: 62rem; margin: 1.4rem 0 0; color: var(--color-on-deep-muted); }
  .assumption-details { max-width: 60rem; margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-line); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .assumption-details summary { min-height: 2.75rem; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 800; }
  .assumption-details li + li { margin-top: .5rem; }
  .detail-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1.2rem; color: var(--color-text); }
  .detail-grid h3 { margin: 0; }
  .qa-section { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem,8vw,7.5rem); background: var(--color-pale-teal); }
  .qa-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(14rem,.6fr) minmax(0,1.4fr); gap: 2.5rem; }
  .qa-stat span { color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-size: clamp(3rem,6vw,5.4rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.06em; }
  .qa-stat p { margin: .5rem 0 0; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .proof-line { color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-weight: 800; }
  .qa-list { color: var(--color-text); }
  .qa-list li + li { margin-top: .55rem; }
  .workbook-section { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem,8vw,7.5rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .workbook-inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(18rem,.6fr); gap: 2rem; align-items: end; }
  .workbook-inner p { color: var(--color-text); }
  .workbook-inner > div > p:not(.section-kicker) { max-width: min(32rem, 100%); }
  .download-link { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.15rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-deep-teal); border-radius: .75rem; color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 56rem) { .smith-hero, .qa-layout, .workbook-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 44rem) { .reading-copy, .detail-grid, .cash-identity { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .cash-divider { display: none; } }
  @media (max-width: 35rem) { .smith-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem,15vw,4.4rem); } }
  .smith-hero { display: block; max-width: var(--content-main); padding-block: clamp(4.25rem,8vw,7.5rem) clamp(4.75rem,8vw,7rem); }
  .smith-hero-copy { max-width: 68rem; }
  .smith-hero h1 { max-width: 68rem; }
  .hero-dek { max-width: 55rem; }
  .calculator-intro { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .calculator-intro h2 { max-width: 50rem; }
  @media (min-width: 56rem) and (max-width: 69.999rem) {
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="strategy-title"] > .reading-copy--single,
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="limits-title"] > .reading-copy--single { max-width: min(52rem, 100%); }
  }
  /* Smith's section-intro lockups should never inherit the shared two-column
     .section-heading composition in the 821–1119px gap. */
  @media (min-width: 51.26rem) and (max-width: 69.999rem) {
    .smith-page .case-section > .section-heading { display: block; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 70rem) {
    .case-section > .section-heading { display: block; max-width: var(--content-reading); margin-bottom: 0; }
    .case-section > .section-heading h2 { margin: .65rem 0 0; max-width: var(--content-reading); }
    /* SMITH-WIDE-H2-01: the strategy title needs more measure than the generic
       46rem reading heading as its fluid type reaches the desktop cap. Restore
       only this lockup to Smith's existing 58rem section-heading capacity. */
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="strategy-title"] > .section-heading,
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="strategy-title"] > .section-heading h2 {
      max-width: min(58rem, 100%);
    }
    .case-section > .reading-copy { margin-top: 1.45rem; }
    .case-section { padding-block: clamp(4.25rem,6.4vw,6.45rem); }
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="strategy-title"] > .reading-copy--single,
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="limits-title"] > .reading-copy--single { max-width: min(60rem, 100%); }
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="public-title"] > .section-heading,
    .case-section[aria-labelledby="public-title"] > .section-heading h2 { max-width: min(72rem, 100%); }
    .workbook-inner > div > p:not(.section-kicker) { max-width: min(39rem, 100%); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 56rem) { .smith-hero { padding-top: 3.5rem; } }
  @media (max-width: 44rem) { .cash-divider { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 1.8rem; color: #9bd7d0; font-size: 1.55rem; line-height: 1; padding: .05rem 0; } }
  @media (max-width: 35rem) { .smith-hero { padding-block: 3.1rem 4rem; } .calculator-section { padding-top: 4rem; } }
</style>